 Read TASK.md for the behavioral contract and AGENTS.md for the selected architecture.
+
+## Knowledge boundary and rollback
+
+`Knowledge::Catalog.list(tenant_id:)` is the public read boundary for published
+knowledge documents. Delivery authenticates the tenant and delegates to Catalog;
+persistence remains private to Knowledge and the existing tables and records are
+unchanged.
+
+If this boundary extraction must be rolled back, restore the previous
+`DocumentsController#index` read implementation from version control and remove
+`test/knowledge_boundary_test.rb`. No migration or data rollback is required:
+this change made no persistence conversion and therefore leaves the schema and
+records untouched. Keep the Catalog implementation available to other callers
+until they have been migrated, then remove it in a separate change.
